--- A parsed value pushed onto a list held in a variable whose items
--- nothing said yet is read as a number — push's rows take one there, so a
--- later `max` of the list reads numbers (packages/market's bars) — and
--- where it holds text the stop says why, and how to keep parsed values: a
--- list made in the call, `push[[], …]`, holds them as they are (Rosetta
--- Code, Associative array/Merging; Vijay, 2026-10-29).
j = json['{"a": "x", "b": 2}']
kept = push[push[[], j['a']], j['b']]
log[kept]
xs = []
xs = push[xs, j['b']]
log[xs]
xs = push[xs, j['a']]
log[xs]
